Description: Offers a broad toolkit for describing, summarising and
    exploring data: frequency and contingency tables, measures of
    location, dispersion, shape and concentration, association and
    agreement coefficients, effect sizes, and metrics for evaluating
    classifiers. A single desc() generic dispatches on the type of the
    input, so univariate, bivariate and whole-data-frame descriptions
    are reached through one consistent entry point. The package is a
    redesigned successor to 'DescTools', with a uniform lowerCamelCase
    API, stricter argument conventions and performance critical parts
    written in C++. It builds on 'bedrock', 'pharos' and 'lumen', which
    supply the base utilities, the graphics and the inferential
    machinery respectively.
